    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26830" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">littĕrālis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lītĕr-</span></b> ),
			e, adj.
		littera, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to letters</i>
			or <i>writing</i> (postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commercium,</span>”
				<i>epistolary correspondence</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 4, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lectio,</span>”
				<i>the reading of books</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grammatica litteralis dicta, quod a litteris
					incipiat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 414</span></i>
			 P.</div>
